        <p class="tagline fade-up fade-up-3">Your own box. Your own data. One command.</p>
    </section>

    {# ============ MOVEMENT 1 · WHY ============ #}
    <section class="section">
        <h2>Why self-host</h2>

        <p>Parachute is a memory you and any AI share &mdash; and self-hosting means that memory lives on a box <em>you</em> control, not a company's servers. It's the whole point:</p>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Own the box.</strong> The hub and vault run on hardware you rent or already own. No account to be locked out of, no service to shut down under you.</li>
            <li><strong>Own the data.</strong> Your notes sit in a database on your disk, in the open. Your AI reads and writes them directly &mdash; nothing round-trips through us.</li>
            <li><strong>No rent to us.</strong> The software is free and open. You pay only for the box it runs on &mdash; from nothing (your own Mac) to a few dollars a month (a small VPS).</li>
            <li><strong>Export anytime.</strong> Your whole vault exports to portable, git-trackable markdown with one command. Leaving is never a migration project.</li>
            <li><strong>No lock-in, ever.</strong> Start on your laptop to try it, move to an always-on box when you're ready &mdash; or hand the running to <a href="https://app.parachute.computer/signup">Parachute Cloud</a> later. Same vault, same stack, your choice.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="muted">Rather not run a box at all? <a href="https://app.parachute.computer/signup">Parachute Cloud</a> is the hosted path &mdash; we run the box, you keep the vault. Everything below is for running it yourself.</p>
    </section>

    {# ============ MOVEMENT 2 · MENTAL MODEL ============ #}
    <section class="section">
        <h2>What you're standing up</h2>

        <p>One picture holds the whole thing. A <strong>hub</strong> supervises everything. Your <strong>vault</strong> &mdash; the knowledge graph your notes and your AI read and write &mdash; is the core. <strong>One command</strong> brings the hub up, and a browser <strong>setup wizard</strong> walks the rest.</p>

        <div class="mm-wrap">
            <div class="mm" role="img" aria-label="One command brings up the hub, which supervises the modules — with the vault as the core — and a setup wizard walks the rest.">
                <div class="mm-cmd"><code>one command</code> <span>&rarr; the hub comes up</span></div>
                <div class="mm-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</div>
